Title: 0007-file-argument-project-directory
Repository: pragtical
Base-Commit: 5c05f09e081833b581fb5ecd10e64963dec87f03
Requires: 0006-aros-volume-parent.patch
Author: aros-pragtical project
Date: 2026-11-01
Upstream-Status: submitted
Upstream-Link: https://github.com/pragtical/pragtical/pull/670
Scope: Startup project selection for file arguments; AROS volume-root reopen.

Problem:
  The command-line file selection independently uses a slash-only parent matcher, leaving project_dir nil for SYS:file.txt even when common.dirname handles that volume.
Solution:
  Use common.dirname for the argument parent and retain the current project if no parent can be determined.
Validation:
  The Pragtical 3.14.0 x86_64 ABIv1 build compiled and linked, and the focused file-argument regression passed three cases. Nested and volume-root command-line reopen checks passed with the expected document contents on 2026-11-15.
Removal:
  Remove when the pinned upstream contains the merged equivalent and the focused regression plus both x86_64 runtime checks pass.

diff --git a/data/core/init.lua b/data/core/init.lua
index 987e1c9f..63a35437 100644
--- a/data/core/init.lua
+++ b/data/core/init.lua
@@ -524,7 +524,7 @@ function core.init()
           end
           if file_abs then
             table.insert(files, file_abs)
-            project_dir = file_abs:match("^(.+)[/\\].+$")
+            project_dir = common.dirname(file_abs) or project_dir
           end
         end
       end
